# Pony ORM Sessions and Transactions Rules

## Always use db_session
- Wrap every DB interaction (reads included) in `@db_session` or `with db_session:` so connections are returned to the pool and the session cache is managed. :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}

## Keep sessions short
- Do not hold a db_session open across slow operations (HTTP calls, large file operations, user prompts).
- Prefer “service function per transaction”: one logical unit of work per db_session.

## Commit and rollback
- Default: let `db_session` commit on success and rollback on exception.
- If you need multiple transactions in one session, call `commit()` or `rollback()` explicitly; the next query starts a new transaction. :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}
- Avoid very long sessions without explicit commits, as they may hold locks longer than intended. :contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}

## Error handling
- Catch exceptions at service boundaries, translate to domain errors, and ensure the exception is not swallowed inside a db_session unless you intentionally recover.
